  "body": "* Bring more than a hammer, probably the whole toolbox.\r\n* Set back from the street at the end of a driveway\r\n* 3 bedrooms, 1 bathroom, 1 living area\r\n* Double garaging with workshop bench\r\n* First time offered since 1974\r\n* 951m² (approx.) freehold site\r\n* Being sold 'as is, where is' - Ignore the CV!\r\n\r\nTo download the property documents, copy & paste this link into your browser: https://www.harcourtsfiles.co.nz/listings/F82K \r\n\r\nSurrounded by mature trees and established planting, this site offers a private and peaceful setting. It's a real opportunity for builders, renovators, potential development or buyers looking to create their own home on a substantial Torbay landholding.\r\n\r\nThe original 1970s home is largely as built and will need extensive work. Anyone considering renovation should approach it as a major project, and many buyers will see removal and a new build as the better option. \r\n\r\nTorbay Village, Waiake Beach and Long Bay Regional Park are all local. Albany and the wider North Shore are within easy reach.\r\n\r\nSo what are you waiting for? Come see it for yourself. Check advertised times, or call today to arrange a private viewing.\r\n\r\nPlease note: this property is being sold \"as is, where is.\" Purchasers are encouraged to seek legal and technical advice and complete their own independent due diligence. That includes reviewing the Record of Title and LIM, and consulting Auckland Council about any proposed future use or development.\r\n\r\nAgent conjunctionals welcome.",
